NAME
       b2sum - print or check BLAKE2b checksums

SYNOPSIS
       b2sum [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       b2sum prints a 512-bit BLAKE2b checksum (128 hexadecimal digits)
       followed by the file name for each FILE, or for standard input when no
       file is given. Two files with the same checksum almost certainly have
       the same contents, so a checksum is a quick way to see whether a copy
       or a download is intact.

       It works like sha256sum and md5sum, only with another algorithm.

EXAMPLES
       Print the checksum of a file:

           b2sum /etc/hosts

SEE ALSO
       sha256sum(1), md5sum(1), cksum(1)
